course: dictionary
lesson: 1285
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it show you which one the writer means. «A butterfly's life cycle is egg, caterpillar, chrysalis and adult butterfly.» Here a butterfly is the insect, because the sentence is about how a living thing grows.
explain: Look at the other words. If someone says they have butterflies in their stomach before a test, the word means a fluttery feeling of nerves, not an insect. If someone says «She swims the butterfly stroke», it is a way of swimming, with both arms moving over the water together.
explain: A social butterfly is a person who moves happily from friend to friend. To check your meaning, put it into the sentence in place of the hard word and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A butterfly is an insect with four large, often brightly coloured wings that flies by day.
fact: The butterfly life cycle has four stages: egg, caterpillar (larva), chrysalis (pupa) and adult butterfly.
fact: Butterflies in your stomach means a fluttery feeling when you are nervous.
fact: Butterfly stroke is a swimming stroke where both arms move over the water together.
fact: A social butterfly is a person who moves happily from friend to friend.
exercise: «A butterfly's life cycle is egg, caterpillar, chrysalis and adult butterfly.» Which stage comes straight after the caterpillar? | Adult butterfly | *Chrysalis | Egg | Tadpole
exercise: Leo says, «I have butterflies in my stomach before the race.» What does he mean? | A swimming stroke | *A fluttery feeling of nerves | An insect with four wings | A friend who likes parties
exercise: «Many animals change shape completely as they grow up: a tadpole becomes a frog, a caterpillar becomes a butterfly.» What is this big change of body called? | Nectar | Butterfly stroke | *Metamorphosis | Proboscis
test: Mia says, «She is a social butterfly.» What does it mean? | A kind of swimming | An insect that flies by day | A fluttery feeling of nerves | *A person who moves happily from friend to friend
test: Which of these names a swimming stroke? | Tadpole | Chrysalis | *Butterfly | Caterpillar
exam: «Longer, unmown grass lets clover, daisies and other flowers bloom and feed bees and butterflies.» Why does longer grass help butterflies? | It stops them from flying | It keeps them dry in the rain | It makes the grass taste sweet | *It lets flowers bloom and gives them food
